ds.\n- Patient currently worried this could be a kidney infection or something more serious.\n\nSynthetic diagnostic tool input:\n1) Urinalysis-support tool:\n- Leukocyte esterase: positive\n- Nitrites: negative\n- Microscopic hematuria: present\n- Protein: trace\n- Interpretation hint: pattern may be compatible with urinary tract inflammation/infection or stone-related irritation; not definitive.\n\n2) Basic vitals triage tool:\n- Temperature: 37.9 C\n- Heart rate: 96 bpm\n- Blood pressure: 146/92\n- Oxygen saturation: 99%\n- Interpretation hint: mild fever and elevated blood pressure; hemodynamically stable.\n\n3) Kidney-risk heuristic tool:\n- Risk flags: dehydration, prior nephrolithiasis, current flank pain\n- Escalation note: urgent in-person assessment is more important if fever rises, vomiting prevents fluids, pain becomes severe, urine output drops, or confusion appears.\n\nPlease produce the final distilled patient-facing report only."},"partialJson":"{\"runtime\":\"subagent\",\"mode\":\"run\",\"cleanup\":\"delete\",\"cwd\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-patient-agent\",\"label\":\"doctor-agent-distill\",\"task\":\"You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent supporting the LoopAI Patient Agent. Run the LLM distillation step conceptually on the following synthetic case context and diagnostic tool input, then return a concise patient-facing output.\\n\\nRequirements:\\n- Do NOT claim this is a confirmed diagnosis.\\n- Clearly distinguish symptom context from tool-derived findings.\\n- Keep uncertainty visible.\\n- Use a clean patient-facing structure.\\n- Include suggested next steps.\\n- End by inviting the user to ask for clarification.\\n\\nSynthetic conversation context:\\n- Adult patient reports 3 days of right-sided flank discomfort, mild nausea, fatigue, and intermittent low-grade fever.\\n- No chest pain, no shortness of breath, no severe bleeding.\\n- Drinking less water than usual over the last week.\\n- History context available to the patient agent: prior episodes of kidney stones; hypertension noted in past records.\\n- Patient currently worried this could be a kidney infection or something more serious.\\n\\nSynthetic diagnostic tool input:\\n1) Urinalysis-support tool:\\n- Leukocyte esterase: positive\\n- Nitrites: negative\\n- Microscopic hematuria: present\\n- Protein: trace\\n- Interpretation hint: pattern may be compatible with urinary tract inflammation/infection or stone-related irritation; not definitive.\\n\\n2) Basic vitals triage tool:\\n- Temperature: 37.9 C\\n- Heart rate: 96 bpm\\n- Blood pressure: 146/92\\n- Oxygen saturation: 99%\\n- Interpretation hint: mild fever and elevated blood pressure; hemodynamically stable.\\n\\n3) Kidney-risk heuristic tool:\\n- Risk flags: dehydration, prior nephrolithiasis, current flank pain\\n- Escalation note: urgent in-person assessment is more important if fever rises, vomiting prevents fluids, pain becomes severe, urine output drops, or confusion appears.\\n\\nPlease produce the final distilled patient-facing report only.\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":402,"output":695,"cacheRead":9472,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":10569,"cost":{"input":0.001005,"output":0.010425,"cacheRead":0.002368,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.013798000000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774459145956}}
